    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d718">

                <pb facs="0747" n="737" xml:id="pg737"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">724.34119/983: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in
                        Argentina</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Weddell</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-08-21T13:00:00-04:00">August 21, 1937—1
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>76. For Braden. Your 147, August 20, 8 p.m. The following telegram has been sent
                    to the Legation at Asunción: (Here quote telegram to Am[erican] Legation,
                        Asunción.<anchor n="19" xml:id="d718-f1"/>)</p>
                <p>Please communicate with Howard by telephone as soon as possible and telegraph the
                    Department the results of your conversation.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
